Bundled third-party code
------------------------

worse_query and pathleak
Copyright (C) 2026 Taj C (forcequit)
https://github.com/forcequitOS/worse_query
License: GPL-3.0

Copied files:
  Bridge/worse_query.h
  Bridge/worse_query.m
  Bridge/pathleak.h
  Bridge/pathleak.m

Bridge/pathleak_range.m and Bridge/pathleak_roots.m are derived from
Bridge/pathleak.m. pathleak_range adds a bounded [from, to] window.
pathleak_roots walks that window once and matches a path against several
container parent prefixes. The path string is built with NSString instead of
NSFileManager. The algorithm and error behaviour otherwise follow the original.

WQ Files (name database and icon technique)
Copyright (C) 2026 kolbicz
https://github.com/kolbicz/WQFiles
License: GPL-3.0-or-later

Bridge/WQNames.m is derived from WQAccess.m in WQ Files. It reads and parses
lsd's CSStore LaunchServices database for app names; the built-in app name
table is copied from the same file.

Bridge/WFLaunchServices.m is adapted from WQLaunchServices.m in WQ Files
(launch-services branch). It parses the same CSStore database for container
paths and app bundle paths, which WorseFiles uses to separate user apps,
system apps and service containers. The parser layouts and bounds checks are
from the original; the WorseFiles access-layer glue was replaced. Bridge/WFInstalledApps.m resolves app
icons through UIKit's private _applicationIconImageForBundleIdentifier method
and rejects iOS's placeholder image using the fingerprint approach from
WQ Files. The technique and parser were adapted, not copied verbatim.

The SwiftUI application, engine, project files, and icon are original work and
